        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1365692?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Since <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3415341892\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/issues/442965\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/NixOS/nixpkgs/pull/442965/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/pull/442965\">#442965</a>, the <code class=\"notranslate\">go run</code> command that <code class=\"notranslate\">libcap</code> does at one point is no longer able to use the linker included in the go compiler, so it uses <code class=\"notranslate\">$CC</code> instead. But <code class=\"notranslate\">libcap</code>'s <code class=\"notranslate\">Makefile</code> uses the wrong compiler for this.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This patch has been submitted to the maintainer upstream. Include it in nixpkgs for now, until it's accepted and a new release is made.</p>\n\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Things done</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li>Built on platform:\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> x86_64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> aarch64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> x86_64-darwin</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-darwin</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Tested, as applicable:\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\"